    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance to help responders locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the access point during nighttime or low-visibility conditions.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along both sides of the driveway so emergency vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Keep the driveway surface clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and debris so responding units can reach the residence without delay.\n• Clear a turnaround area near the residence or detached structure large enough for a fire engine or ambulance to reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Cut back dense vegetation where it meets the driveway edges to prevent it from narrowing the usable travel width for large vehicles.\n• Keep a gate or barrier at the driveway entrance unlocked or equipped with a Knox Box so responders can enter without delay.\n• Mark the detached structure with a visible identifier so responding crews can distinguish it from the main residence when staging or searching the property.\n• Thin dense vegetation between the main residence and detached structure to give responders a clear path between the two buildings."
  },
