    "recommendations": "• Thin scattered trees nearest to the structure to increase open space between the tree canopy and the building.\n• Trim shrubs growing close to the structure's exterior walls and foundation.\n• Cut or mow grass cover in the immediate area around the structure to reduce low-level fire spread toward the building.\n• Remove any shrubs or small trees growing directly against the structure.\n• Separate clusters of shrubs from one another by removing or thinning vegetation between groupings near the structure.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of overhanging branches so emergency vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along both sides of the driveway to maintain a clear travel lane.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is visible to emergency responders approaching from the road.\n• Clear vegetation from the rear of the structure to allow movement and access around the building.\n• Mow or cut grass along the driveway edges to reduce the path by which fire could travel toward the structure.\n• Remove dead branches from trees near the structure, particularly on the sides facing heaviest vegetation.\n• Keep the area immediately surrounding any outbuildings or improvements clear of shrubs and tall grass."
